  "term": "dissociative identity disorder",
  "definition": "Dissociative identity disorder is a dissociative disorder in which one person has two or more distinct personalities. These personalities are described as complex and integrated, with their own memories, behavior patterns, and social relationships, and shifts between them happen suddenly.",
